  <revision rev="3" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>cb930f7cae1edef259e96dd932e0a95f</srcmd5>
    <version>5.5.0</version>
    <time>1767882358</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>- Add libdir-luaconf.patch making it possible for the build
  process to be driven only by the command line arguments of
  `make` without a need to modify `src/luaconf.h` &quot;manually&quot;.
- Add 32bit-check.patch to fix failed tests on 32bit platforms,
  to fix 32-bit integer overflow in str_rep function.

- Update to the final release of 5.5.0, overview of the main
  changes for this major version:
  - declarations for global variables
  - named vararg tables
  - for-loop variables are read only
  - floats are printed in decimal with enough digits to be read
    back correctly.
  - more levels for constructors
  - table.create
  - utf8.offset returns also final position of character
  - external strings (that use memory not managed by Lua)
  - new functions luaL_openselectedlibs and luaL_makeseed
  - major garbage collections done incrementally
  - more compact arrays (large arrays use about 60% less memory)
  - lua.c loads 'readline' dynamically
  - static (fixed) binaries (when loading a binary chunk in
    memory, Lua can reuse its original memory in some of the
    internal structures)
  - dump and undump reuse all strings
  - auxiliary buffer reuses buffer when it creates final string 

- Update to 5.5.0-rc1:
  bugfixes</comment>
    <requestid>1325525</requestid>
  </revision>
  <revision rev="4" vrev="2">
    <srcmd5>c852032cd53b2c525b3652d918e42544</srcmd5>
    <version>5.5.0</version>
    <time>1795519347</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Series of fixes to finish updating lua55 package

- Fix the spec file, which did not parse at all: the conditional
  around the scriptlets was never closed.
- Define the libalternatives build conditional (as lua54 does).
  It was used but never defined, so the package always took the
  update-alternatives branch while requiring alts and lacking the
  update-alternatives scriptlet dependencies.
- Link readline directly. With the plain linux target lua.c tries
  to dlopen &quot;libreadline.so&quot;, which only readline-devel provides,
  so the interactive interpreter ran without line editing.
- Drop the test flavour. The check section of the main build now
  runs the upstream test suite against the staged installation in
  the build root and verifies that the compiled-in search paths
  match INSTALL_LMOD and INSTALL_CMOD in lua5.5.pc.
- Remove the unused BuildRequires on lua-macros.

- Support update-alternatives when libalternatives is disabled,
  including command and man page links and registration scriptlets.
- Ignore lua55 during dependency resolution to allow building
  without an already installed copy of the package.</comment>
    <requestid>1399816</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
